Quartic girth-six lambda20: exact lower36
=======================================

This is one bounded F012 lower-bound clause, not whole-paper recovery. Lambda19, printed in the same source row, remains separate.

Fresh complete replay (about five minutes):

  python check.py --study STUDY --out NEW_DIRECTORY --render

Requires Python3, C++17 clang++, 64-bit-word nauty headers/library at the standard Homebrew locations, and (for rendering) pdflatex, Ghostscript and pypdf. The mathematical verification uses only local numeric inputs. --study additionally rehashes acquired documentary/proof bindings. Exact historical compiler/library bytes are recorded, not substituted for the fresh executable.

--sanitize compiles address/undefined-instrumented executables (allow up to25minutes). Unsupported macOS leak detection is disabled; address/undefined checks remain enabled. --reuse-recorded-root explicitly reuses the complete root execution after full exact input/output closure validation; all other controls and extensions still run fresh. This differs from a fresh root replay and is labelled in the report. No private runtime fallback or eight-gigabyte diagnostic trace is required.

The guarded literal maps are authoritative. Nauty supplies target hints only; a missed or false map aborts. First-side partitions, all partial joins and the order35 final boundary are exhausted by the standalone C++ code.
